WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:15.828
It was Friday, and Bobby felt like he might explode.

2
00:00:15.829 --> 00:00:18.370
He couldn't wait for the weekend.

3
00:00:18.371 --> 00:00:25.725
He was going to see a football game with his dad on Sunday!

4
00:00:25.726 --> 00:00:27.365
"I brought my bottle,"

5
00:00:27.366 --> 00:00:30.305
he said as he walked into Kids Central.

6
00:00:30.306 --> 00:00:32.965
"Great," Miss Shelly said.

7
00:00:32.967 --> 00:00:36.945
"Then get ready to make a sugar and yeast balloon."

8
00:00:36.946 --> 00:00:42.157
"Whatever that is, it sounds cool!" Bobby said.

9
00:00:42.158 --> 00:00:45.149
"You know sugar gives you energy, right?

10
00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:51.523
We're going to give yeast some sugar," Miss Shelly said.

11
00:00:51.524 --> 00:00:53.982
"What do you think will happen?

12
00:00:53.983 --> 00:00:57.612
Will the sugar and yeast blow up our balloons?"

13
00:00:57.613 --> 00:01:00.679
Miss Shelly blew air into a balloon.

14
00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:06.103
"Or not?" She let out all the air.

15
00:01:06.104 --> 00:01:09.739
"Yeast makes bread rise," Jason said.

16
00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:15.512
"So I think yes, it will make our balloons blow up."

17
00:01:15.513 --> 00:01:20.463
"How can sugar and yeast blow up a balloon?" Bobby asked.

18
00:01:20.464 --> 00:01:22.212
He shook his head.

19
00:01:22.213 --> 00:01:24.940
"I don't think it will work."

20
00:01:24.941 --> 00:01:28.925
"Let's try and find out," Miss Shelly said.

21
00:01:28.926 --> 00:01:32.513
"Drop one tablespoon of sugar into your bottle.

22
00:01:32.514 --> 00:01:37.162
I'll come around with warm water."

23
00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:42.136
Bobby carefully spooned the sugar into his bottle.

24
00:01:42.137 --> 00:01:44.657
He shot his arm up in the air.

25
00:01:44.658 --> 00:01:47.944
"I'm ready for water, Miss Shelly!"

26
00:01:47.945 --> 00:01:51.567
Miss Shelly poured warm water into his bottle.

27
00:01:51.568 --> 00:01:54.439
"Now shake!" she said.

28
00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:57.121
Bobby shook as hard as he could.

29
00:01:57.122 --> 00:01:59.450
"That's good enough, Bobby.

30
00:01:59.451 --> 00:02:01.706
Next add the yeast.

31
00:02:01.707 --> 00:02:04.073
Then put the balloon on.

32
00:02:04.074 --> 00:02:06.890
Gently shake it up!"

33
00:02:06.891 --> 00:02:10.468
Bobby emptied the packet of yeast into the bottle.

34
00:02:10.469 --> 00:02:13.755
He put a blue balloon on the top of the bottle.

35
00:02:13.756 --> 00:02:20.467
Then he shook the bottle again, gently.

36
00:02:20.468 --> 00:02:23.899
"Nothing's happening," he complained.

37
00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:27.179
"Be patient," Miss Shelly said.

38
00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:39.714
"Let's go outside while we wait."

39
00:02:39.715 --> 00:02:43.488
"Oh!" Izzie shrieked when they got back.

40
00:02:43.489 --> 00:02:46.326
"My balloon is getting bigger!"

41
00:02:46.327 --> 00:02:50.228
Everyone ran to Izzie's bottle on the table.

42
00:02:50.229 --> 00:02:52.572
Bobby dashed to his seat.

43
00:02:52.573 --> 00:02:57.981
"Mine's growing too!"

44
00:02:57.982 --> 00:03:00.220
"That is so weird,"

45
00:03:00.221 --> 00:03:03.600
Jason said, examining his own balloon.

46
00:03:03.601 --> 00:03:07.013
"Who's blowing it up?" Nina asked.

47
00:03:07.014 --> 00:03:10.932
"How is it getting bigger?"

48
00:03:10.933 --> 00:03:16.365
"The sugar and the yeast are doing it.

49
00:03:16.366 --> 00:03:20.862
Yeast is actually alive, you see.

50
00:03:20.863 --> 00:03:24.747
But it's in a quiet, sleeping stage in the packet.

51
00:03:24.748 --> 00:03:26.681
When mixed with water and sugar, it becomes active again," Miss Shelly explained.

52
00:03:30.594 --> 00:03:35.568
"When yeast eats sugar, it creates gas that fills the balloon.

53
00:03:35.569 --> 00:03:39.071
The balloon gets bigger to make room for the gas.

54
00:03:39.072 --> 00:03:42.621
Just like it gets bigger when we blow into it!

55
00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:46.434
Does that make sense?" Miss Shelly asked.

56
00:03:46.435 --> 00:03:49.666
A tall man entered the gym.

57
00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:53.693
"What's going on in here?" he asked.

58
00:03:53.694 --> 00:03:57.967
"Dad! Look at this!" Bobby shouted.

59
00:03:57.968 --> 00:04:02.473
"We mixed yeast, sugar, and water in a bottle.

60
00:04:02.474 --> 00:04:06.748
That created gas that blew up this balloon!"

61
00:04:06.749 --> 00:04:10.082
"That sounds interesting," Bobby's dad said.

62
00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:17.311
"And in a few hours, you'll see what happens when the yeast runs out of sugar to eat," Miss Shelly said.

63
00:04:17.312 --> 00:04:21.912
"What? You mean there's more?" Bobby asked.

64
00:04:21.913 --> 00:04:26.261
"Take your balloon home, and we'll watch it there," his dad said.

65
00:04:26.262 --> 00:04:29.370
Bobby was thrilled.

66
00:04:29.371 --> 00:04:33.481
He'd get to watch football and his balloon with his dad.

67
00:04:33.482 --> 00:04:40.001
It was going to be a great weekend!
